# Every text file is LF in the repository *and* in the working copy, on every machine.
# Without the `eol=lf` half, Git hands Windows a CRLF checkout while Prettier
# (`"endOfLine": "lf"`) writes LF back, so a single `pnpm format` marks the whole tree as
# modified with no content change at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Orval-generated client is verified in CI with `git diff --exit-code` after `pnpm gen`.
# It is excluded from Prettier, so it needs the rule stated for itself — the line above would
# cover it today, but this one survives a future `text=auto` change.
packages/api-client/** text eol=lf
